Z||000004||RZURCTN||02-11-2000||11:38 PM||||Thanks for the answers!  I'm not installing a subwoofer, just a couple of 6x9's.  I wanted to kow if I would have to extend the firewall, or if I could just cut a hole and drop them in.  Sounds like cutting the hole will work!  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierosound||02-12-2000||02:07 AM||||Even if you cut a hole just big enough to fit the 6x9, you will have to seal the ends of the channels.  This can be done from underneath the car.  If you don't do this, water could get up in there and ruin your speakers.  Also, your music will be heard outside, sounding like you have speakers in your engine!<P>PYLE DRIVER makes a great sounding 6x9 that puts out alot of bass.  Make sure to get good speakers up front and tune your system (you are getting an equalizer aren't you?) properly, otherwise it'll sound like the band is playing the music behind you!  That's not what you want!  You want to get the illusion of "front row, center" when you hear the music.  That why the factory setup has better speakers up front than in the rear.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 02-12-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000006||RZURCTN||02-12-2000||01:56 PM||||When I listen to my music I prefer to feel like I am on center stage!  Right in the middle of it all.  <BR>Thanks for telling me about sealing the channel.  I wouldn't have known.  Currently I have Panasonic 2-way 4x10's in the front.  They are good quality speakers and sound great.  I like the speakers in the headrests, but they don't put out enough for me.  I have a "Road Gear" stereo and 6x9's from Wal-mart.  Don't laugh either!  I got the set which retails at $69.00 for only $10.00!  Not bad, and it's only a temporary solution for longterm tunage.  ||||reg||1
